NOTES ____________________________

Branches & tags are LOCAL until you push. GitHub won’t show them until you send them.

Check what you have locally

Show branch: git branch --show-current

List branches: git branch -a

List tags: git tag --list

Remote set?: git remote -v

Push your branch (dev)

First time: git push -u origin dev

Later: git push

Push your tag(s)

One tag: git push origin <your-tag-name>

All tags: git push --tags

Verify on GitHub

Refresh repo page → Branches tab shows dev

Tags tab shows your tag(s). (If you used a different name than you think, run git tag --list to confirm.)

If still not showing

Confirm remote URL: git remote -v (matches your GitHub repo)

See what GitHub has: git ls-remote --heads --tags origin

Make sure tag has no spaces and is exactly the one you pushed.

Typical flow (copy-paste)

git branch --show-current
git remote -v
git push -u origin dev
git tag --list
git push origin v2025.10.20-menu-clean   # or: git push --tags

